<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James II of Scotland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1430">1430</a>–<a href="/years/1460">1460</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James II was King of Scots from 1437 to 1460, known for the red birthmark on his face. After a minority dominated by noble factions, he broke the power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clan-douglas">Black Douglases</a>, killing the eighth earl in 1452. An enthusiast for artillery, he was killed in 1460 when one of his own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannons</a> burst during the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roxburgh-castle">Roxburgh Castle</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-scotland.jpg" alt="James II of Scotland" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author to Georg (Jörg) von Ehingen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_II_of_Scotland_(by_von_Ehingen).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
